  "text": "Stage 8 isn't clean yet. The build passes, but the `stale` check still fails, and that failure isn't one I can clear from this stage.\n\n- **Build:** the route build passes every stage gate. WNS is 2.59 ns, TNS 0.0, WHS 0.012 ns and THS 0.0. Resources are 393 LUT, 1196 FF, 0.5 BRAM and 0 DSP. The DRC, methodology and CDC gates are clean, and a bitstream was produced.\n- **`stale` check fails (HDL-ORC-02):** `build/sim` is older than the current `design.xdc`. Clearing it needs the simulation re-run, and this stage doesn't allow that. The build said \"cache hit, Vivado not run\", so the route build was not re-run on the new constraints.\n- **Partial or not-run checks:**\n  - `clocking`, `init_values`, `control_sets` and `clock_mux` didn't finish because another Vivado job was running (limit `FDA_VIVADO_MAX=1`).\n  - `fastpath` is also listed as not run; I didn't look into why.\n  - I didn't re-run them, so they are unverified rather than passing.\n- **Warnings recorded, not gates:** several `CDCM-MTBF-LOW` entries, one `CDCM-DPO-LOOSE`, and an `async_clock_groups_review` warning between `usr_cclk` and `sys_clk_pin`.\n\nDONE"
